hypotheses.statement:
In the commutative ring $K_0(\mathcal C)/pK_0(\mathcal C)$, one has $$[Y]^p=\sum_{i=1}^{p-1}i[F_i(Y)].$$ Consequently, for every $r\geq1$, $$\label{eq:iterated-ordinary-congruence}
 [Y]^{p^r}
 =\sum_{i_1,\ldots,i_r=1}^{p-1}
    (i_1\cdots i_r)
    [F_{i_r}\cdots F_{i_1}(Y)]
 \pmod p.$$

outputs.exact_statement:
Let $\alpha_1,\ldots,\alpha_r\in k$ be linearly independent over $\mathbb F_p$. There are $\mathbb F_p$-linearly independent $\lambda_1,\ldots,\lambda_r\in k$ such that $$\label{eq:selected-embedding}
 \sum_{i=1}^r\alpha_i\lambda_i^{p^j}=0
 \qquad(0\le j\le r-2).$$ For $r=1$ the list of equations is empty.

